        <mxCell id="s3o6uzVczVroYJs5pFii-29" parent="1" style="triangle;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shapeInside=1;strokeColor=#457B9D;fontColor=#1D3557;fillColor=#A8DADC;rotation=-180;labelBackgroundColor=none;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="10" width="10" x="350" y="883" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3o6uzVczVroYJs5pFii-30" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontColor=#1D3557;labelBackgroundColor=none;" value="Notes from Duc:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(29, 53, 87), rgb(176, 196, 226));&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;- Changed the Role entity to three distinct entities (Seller, Buyer, Admin) as subclass, and UserAccount as Superclass.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(29, 53, 87), rgb(176, 196, 226));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(29, 53, 87), rgb(176, 196, 226));&quot;&gt;- Didn&#39;t include ItemCategories entity as it&#39;s too convoluted for ER diagram. Will still be needed in schema.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(29, 53, 87), rgb(176, 196, 226));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(29, 53, 87), rgb(176, 196, 226));&quot;&gt;- Buyer follows Seller is now a relationship for simplicity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(29, 53, 87), rgb(176, 196, 226));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Notification type follows same simplified pattern as above. Added isEnabling show the Attributes on Relationship.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Same with Buyer--Watches--&amp;gt;Auction&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Not sure whether Notification--Received By--&amp;gt;1..* UserAccount. I think in our design receiverID stops this. Intuitively, having shared notifications makes more sense to me, instead of duplicating notifications. I&#39;ve written Notification --&amp;gt;1..* User Accounts instead. Happy t0 change&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Have put outcome type as an attribute of Outcome. Not sure whether we should keep the outcome type a separate table, like our schema, or whether this is better for ER.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- In this particular diagram, there&#39;s no&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;buy-now == winning bid &lt;/b&gt;if winning bid matches&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;- &lt;/b&gt;We have bidderId {FK} in Bids entity, would that be an issue since the ER does not specify a bidderId&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="450" width="430" x="-710" y="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3o6uzVczVroYJs5pFii-32" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontColor=#1D3557;labelBackgroundColor=none;" value="Classifies" vertex="1">
